    <section class="policy-section" id="who-we-are" aria-labelledby="label-who">
      <div class="section-label" id="label-who">01 · Who we are</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>Refueler (incorporating as Refueler Ltd, England &amp; Wales) is the data controller for the personal data described here.</p>
        <p>We are registered with the Information Commissioner's Office. Our ICO registration number will be displayed here prior to this policy going live.</p>
        <p><strong>Processors</strong></p>
        <div class="inset-card">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Processor</th>
                <th>Role</th>
                <th>Region</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Cloudflare</td>
                <td>Hosting, file storage for Share, the check that a visitor is a person, and Share sign-in emails</td>
                <td>Global</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Supabase</td>
                <td>Database for Share Citizen accounts</td>
                <td>EU (Ireland)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Stripe</td>
                <td>Card payments, for paying Share Citizens only</td>
                <td>Global</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>Each works under its Data Processing Agreement. These three are all of them. Cloudflare and Stripe may handle data outside the UK; this is covered by the safeguards in their agreements.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-section" id="share" aria-labelledby="label-share">
      <div class="section-label" id="label-share">02 · Refueler Share</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>Share, at share.refueler.io, encrypts your files in your browser before they leave it. The key travels in the part of the link after <code>#</code>, which browsers do not send to any server. We cannot open your files or read their names.</p>
        <p>What Share keeps:</p>
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Data</th>
              <th>Why</th>
              <th>Where</th>
              <th>How long</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Encrypted pieces of your files, and their stored size</td>
              <td>Deliver them to your receiver</td>
              <td>Cloudflare</td>
              <td>Until the transfer expires or is deleted</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>A transfer id, when it was sent and when it expires</td>
              <td>Find the transfer and end it on time</td>
              <td>Cloudflare</td>
              <td>Until it ends; then only the id and the time it ended, so the link can say it has gone</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Short error notes: a step name, a status code, part of a transfer id</td>
              <td>Find and fix what breaks</td>
              <td>Cloudflare</td>
              <td>Up to 90 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Citizens only: email address, Stripe customer reference, plan and renewal date</td>
              <td>Sign-in and your plan</td>
              <td>Supabase (EU, Ireland)</td>
              <td>While you are a Citizen</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Citizens only: when you signed in, to the minute, kept as one-way fingerprints</td>
              <td>Keep you signed in</td>
              <td>Supabase (EU, Ireland)</td>
              <td>24 hours at most</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>Error notes never hold file names, keys, your IP address or your browser. Sign-in records hold no IP address, device or location.</p>
        <p><strong>Others who play a part:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> runs the servers, so it sees your IP address as any host does. Before an upload it runs a short check that you are a person, which reads signals from your browser inside Cloudflare's own frame. It also sends Citizens' sign-in emails; each link works once, for 15 minutes.</li>
          <li><strong>Stripe</strong> takes card payments for paying Citizens only. We never see your card.</li>
          <li><strong>OpenTimestamps</strong> calendar servers receive a one-way fingerprint only if you choose a permanent record (paid plans). It reveals nothing about your file. They see your IP address as any server does.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Share runs no analytics, advertising or tracking script. Visit numbers come only from Cloudflare's own traffic totals as our host.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-section" id="cookies" aria-labelledby="label-cookies">
      <div class="section-label" id="label-cookies">03 · Cookies</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>A few small cookies, each with one job:</p>
        <div class="inset-card">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Cookie</th>
                <th>What it does</th>
                <th>Lasts</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>__Host-rfs_session</code></td>
                <td>Keeps you signed in to Share as a Citizen. Set only when you sign in</td>
                <td>Ends after 1 hour unused, 24 hours at most</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>__cf_bm</code>, <code>cf_clearance</code></td>
                <td>Set by Cloudflare, our host, only when it needs to tell people from automated traffic</td>
                <td><code>__cf_bm</code> 30 minutes; <code>cf_clearance</code> after a check</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>__stripe_mid</code>, <code>__stripe_sid</code></td>
                <td>Set by Stripe, our card processor, on Share's Plans pages, and only once you start a payment. They help Stripe stop card fraud</td>
                <td><code>__stripe_mid</code> 1 year; <code>__stripe_sid</code> 30 minutes</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>These, and nothing for advertising or tracking across sites.</p>
        <p>Some choices stay in your own browser and are never sent to us: Paper or Carbon, the notes that let an interrupted upload carry on, and whether you have seen a notice (cleared when you close the tab).</p>
        <p>You can check this yourself: your browser's developer tools → Storage (or Application) → Cookies.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-section" id="website" aria-labelledby="label-website">
      <div class="section-label" id="label-website">04 · This website</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>refueler.io pages, though not Share, count visits with our own counter: the page, the site you came from, your country, whether you are on a phone or a computer, the theme and how far you read. It sets no cookie and keeps no IP address.</p>
        <p>These pages also load fonts from Google Fonts and Fontshare, which see your IP address as any host does. Share loads its fonts from its own server.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-section" id="legal-basis" aria-labelledby="label-legal">
      <div class="section-label" id="label-legal">
        05 · Legal basis
        <span class="label-sub">UK GDPR Art. 6</span>
      </div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Activity</th>
              <th>Legal basis</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Sending and receiving a transfer you asked for</td><td>Art. 6(1)(b) — performance of contract</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Citizen sign-in, plan and payment</td><td>Art. 6(1)(b) — performance of contract</td></tr>
            <tr><td>The check that you are a person, and error notes</td><td>Art. 6(1)(f) — legitimate interests: keeping the service safe and working</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Counting visits to refueler.io pages</td><td>Art. 6(1)(f) — legitimate interests: knowing which pages are read</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-section" id="your-rights" aria-labelledby="label-rights">
      <div class="section-label" id="label-rights">
        06 · Your rights
        <span class="label-sub">UK GDPR Arts. 15–22</span>
      </div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>You can ask us to show, correct, export or delete what we hold about you, to pause its use, or to stop a use that rests on legitimate interests. Email <a href="mailto:privacy@refueler.io">privacy@refueler.io</a>. We reply within 30 days, usually much sooner.</p>
        <div class="inset-card">
          <p><strong>Citizens.</strong> To delete your account, email us for now; a Delete account option is coming to your account page.</p>
          <p><strong>Free transfers</strong> are not linked to you. To have one removed before it expires, send us the link up to the <code>#</code> — never the part after it, which is the key.</p>
        </div>
        <p>No decision with legal or similar effect is made about you automatically.</p>
        <div class="ico-block">
          <p><strong>Right to complain to the ICO</strong></p>
          <p>If you believe we have handled your personal data unlawfully, you have the right to lodge a complaint with the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) under Article 77 of the UK GDPR.</p>
          <p>ICO website: <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; Helpline: 0303 123 1113</p>
          <p>We would always prefer the chance to put things right first — please write to <a href="mailto:privacy@refueler.io">privacy@refueler.io</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-section" id="changes" aria-labelledby="label-changes">
      <div class="section-label" id="label-changes">07 · Changes to this policy</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>We check this page against the live services on a regular schedule. The dates at the top say when it last changed and when it was last checked.</p>
        <p>Material changes — new kinds of data, new processors, new legal bases, longer retention — are announced on the Share status page before they take effect. Version history is kept in a private Git repository.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

